e_fcf_yield":0.16624423762179474,"_gp_fcf_yield":true,"_score_fcf_yield":100.0,"_gate_int_coverage":6.269822485207101,"_gp_int_coverage":true,"_score_int_coverage":27.7,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":1.4671554691007034,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":56.3,"_gate_accruals":-0.03857475303219443,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":36.9,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.07411407667298621,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":93.1,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.01255953640099898,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":84.3,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":0.09563609026495117,"_gp_spread":true,"_score_spread":47.8,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.61409278022673,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.21786956989021436,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":89.3,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.05680802533223524,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":52.3,"_gate_pool_share":0.39300551093706515,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.09125636926227276,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":70.6,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.22744363483693575,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":-0.0034627579898144135,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":46.5,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.003135130892704896,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":53.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.012982423071485793,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":78.4,"_gate_insider_own":0.07339,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":48.9,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":["paper"],"description_full":"Euronet Worldwide, Inc. provides payment and transaction processing and distribution solutions to financial institutions, retailers, service providers, and individual consumers internationally. The company operates through three segments: Electronic Funds Transfer (EFT), epay, and Money Transfer. The EFT segment provides automated teller machine cash withdrawal and deposit services, ATM network participation, outsourced ATM and point-of-sale (POS) management solutions, credit and debit and prepaid card outsourcing, card issuing, and merchant acquiring services. It also offers ATM and POS dynamic currency conversion, domestic and international surcharge, foreign currency dispensing, advertising, digital content sales at ATMs, customer relationship management, prepaid mobile top-up, bill payment, money transfer, fraud management, foreign remittance payout, cardless payout, banknote recycling solutions, and tax-refund services; and integrated electronic financial transaction software solutions for electronic payment and transaction delivery systems. The epay segment distributes and processes prepaid mobile airtime and other electronic content and payment processing services for various prepaid products, cards, and services. The Money Transfer segment offers consumer-to-consumer money transfer services through a network of locations and its website riamoneytransfer.com; account-to-account money transfer; and money transfer services through its website xe.com, Xe app, and customer service representatives. It also provides foreign currency exchange information on its currency data websites xe.com and x-rates.com; cash management solutions and foreign currency risk management services to small-and-medium-sized businesses; and payment processing services to third-party partners. The company was formerly known as Euronet Services, Inc. and changed its name to Euronet Worldwide, Inc. in August 2001. The company was founded in 1994 and is headquartered in Leawood, Kansas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael J. Brown M.Sc. | Chairman, CEO & President | Age 68 | Compensation: $2.8M (FY2016)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 10K people. Revenue per employee of $393K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 10%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $40K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Euronet Worldwide, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $2.6B market cap on $4.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 8% cost of capital, a 10-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $434M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.81\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.5\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 6.3\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 7.3% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 73% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 72% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(EEFT) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/23/EEFT_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_111026101201_1794366721.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794366721.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Euronet Worldwide (EEFT) Faces A Fresh Valuation Test Following Earnings Cut And ATM Deal","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nasdaq-eeft/euronet-worldwide/news/euronet-worldwide-eeft-faces-a-fresh-valuation-test-followin","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794137582.734,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.468,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Euronet Worldwide (EEFT) Could Be 25% Undervalued Following Lower 2026 Guidance","